  "source": {
    "plan": "Callboard row 2026-11-27 (storyhowto, story-howto), the earliest planned row on 2026-11-22; look collage per DIRECTION 2026-11-20 (the row said bold)",
    "project": "ppvqmbzuqvzpiuqaiqfy",
    "sql": "select m.*, p.* from monologues m join plays p on p.id=m.play_id where p.title in ('Are you ready?','American Magic','The Audition','My Own Personal Mermaid')",
    "checked": "2026-11-22: monologue 44218 Woman (Are you ready?, David Auburn, play 3515, 2001, copyrighted, fair_use, source_url set) 2:37; 45293 Woman (American Magic, Gil Kofman, play 4147, 2008) 2:34; Elizabeth (The Audition, Don Zolidis) 1:41. In the Ghost Light app 'contemporary theatre monologue for a woman in her twenties' returns these three first, 30 monologues",
    "changed_from_plan": "the row's search ('contemporary, a woman in her twenties, two minutes') puts film cards with posters first in the app (Her, Source Code, Broadcast News), so the film types a wording that brings three contemporary plays up first. The app shows play and playwright, not the year, so no year is claimed. These are copyrighted: the speech text on the results cards, the opened page and Tonight's speech (Mags, My Own Personal Mermaid) is blurred in the screenshots; names, plays, playwrights and lengths stay sharp",
    "app": "Ghost Light web preview built from actorrise main apps/mobile (ed12f1ed) plus web-preview.patch, dark theme, demo account, 2026-11-22",
    "flow": "flows/search-asked-for-contemporary.json (shots -> public/story/2026-11-27-asked-for-contemporary/*.png)",
    "voice": "George, one take at stability 0.5, Scribe 0.99, sped up 1.25x with fit_take.py; AI voice, labelled on every platform",
    "new_scene_types": "libdesk (cut-paper collage) with three beats: hook, ask, pile. New collage pieces: LibraryWall (shelves of paper spines), LibraryDesk, PBook, dust puffs, the scarf caught under Shakespeare",
